---
description: Safety guardrails for an existing repository
alwaysApply: true
---

Safety rules:
- prefer minimal safe diffs
- do not rewrite architecture unnecessarily
- do not rename or move large sets of files without clear justification
- do not remove code without checking references and usage
- preserve existing behavior unless explicitly asked to change it
- explain larger refactors before implementing them
- prefer incremental improvements over full rewrites
- do not invent libraries, APIs, database fields, or environment variables